//@version=6
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  KASAUTI · कसौटी  ·  CALIBRATED RISK, EXPOSURE AND SELF-AUDIT              v2.1
//  "How far can it go, how much should I hold - and has that been true here?"
//
//  Kasauti is the touchstone: the black stone a goldsmith rubs metal on to see
//  what it is. This script forecasts only what the data says can be forecast,
//  states every forecast as a probability, and then tests itself on the chart.
//
//  ONE SCRIPT. Everything - the pane, the tapes, the cone and stops, the
//  volume profile and the table - is this one indicator. The only data it
//  requests is the chart symbol's own lower timeframe, for the profile.
//
//  v2.1 · THE VOLUME PROFILE, carried in whole from Pragati (section 7): the
//  session histogram with POC and value area, VWAP, Initial Balance, prior-
//  session levels and naked POCs. Display only - nothing in the risk engine,
//  the cone, the stops, the dial or the ledger reads it. It sits to the right
//  of the forward cone, and the cone's and stops' tags share its tag column.
//  No engine number changed from v2.0.
//
//  WHY IT IS NOT A DIRECTION ORACLE. Measured first (research/, 151 instruments
//  in seven classes, daily bars 2001-2026, three eras): no price or volume
//  state tried - trend, stretch, dips, volume, overnight against session,
//  efficiency - led the next 10 bars in a way that held in all three eras.
//  What IS forecastable is RISK: the next 10 bars' variance is predicted out
//  of sample with a log R² of 0.71. So this script forecasts risk and turns it
//  into the three numbers a position needs: how far, how much, where it is
//  wrong.
//
//  ═══ WHAT IS ON THE PANE, TOP TO BOTTOM ═══════════════════════════════════
//      +5.6  STRETCH LADDER    how many horizons call this move a surprise
//      +4.9  TREND TAPE        the move over a quarter, a half, a year - in σ
//      +q    upper band        the learned edge of the cone
//        0   SURPRISE          the realised H-bar move ÷ the forecast made H
//                              bars ago; columns coloured by trend
//      −q    lower band
//      −4.9  RISK TAPE         calm · normal · stressed
//      −5.6  RISK MOMENTUM     risk rising · steady · falling
//
//  ON THE PRICE CHART: the CONE forward from the last bar, the long and short
//  STOPS across it, the LANDING band - the cone drawn H bars ago, at today's
//  bar - the VOLUME PROFILE to the cone's right, and the table.
//
//  ═══ THE TAPES · WHAT EACH ONE CHANGES ════════════════════════════════════
//  A tape is here only if a number depends on it. The two inner tapes are the
//  two things the cone and the dial LISTEN to; the two outer tapes say where
//  each is heading.
//
//  TREND (+4.9)   green up, red down, faint while flat (inside ±0.5σ).
//      · It SKEWS THE CONE. Before the cone listened to it, a short stop in a
//        downtrend was touched 27% of the time against a stated 20%, and a
//        long stop in an uptrend 22%. With it: 21% and 20%.
//      · It is the dial's THROTTLE and the ledger's row.
//  STRETCH LADDER (+5.6)   the surprise at four horizons - H/2, H, 2H, 4H -
//      each against its OWN learned cone. Hue: the side. Intensity: how many
//      rungs are outside - faint none, clear one or two, solid three or four.
//      · Three or four rungs outside happens on about 4% of bars a side.
//      · It carries NO direction (measured, all three eras).
//      · After a ladder-wide break BELOW, a long stop is touched about a
//        quarter of the time, not a fifth - the one place the stops still
//        understate. The table's LONG STOP row turns gold there.
//  RISK (−4.9)    blue calm, grey normal, gold stressed - where forecast risk
//      stands among its last 500 bars.
//      · It sets the cone's WIDTH term and the dial's first factor.
//      · Stressed risk fell over the next 10 bars (median −8%); calm risk did
//        not rise (+1%). Stress fades; calm persists.
//  RISK MOMENTUM (−5.6)   gold rising, blue falling, faint steady - the change
//      in forecast risk over the last H bars, past ±10%.
//      · RISING is a spike, and spikes fade: risk was LOWER 10 bars later 74%
//        of the time (median −11%), in every era. A cone drawn into a spike
//        is at its widest.
//
//  GOLD, everywhere here, means risk - never up or down.
//
//  ═══ HOW IT WORKS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//    RISK      per-bar variance from the bar's whole range and its gap
//              (Garman-Klass), blended over three horizons - 0.25 · 5-bar +
//              0.40 · 22-bar + 0.35 · 252-bar - and rescaled to close-to-close.
//              Beats a 20-bar standard deviation by 30% (QLIKE) out of sample.
//    CONE      close · exp(± q · σ · √H). q is not a normal quantile: it is
//              LEARNED. Every bar the forecast made H bars ago is settled; a
//              miss widens q, a hit narrows it, in the ratio that makes the
//              miss rate converge on the target (adaptive conformal
//              inference). log q = a term for the risk regime + a term for
//              the trend state, each side separately - so fat tails and skew
//              are measured, not assumed.
//    STOPS     the same, settled on the lowest low (highest high) of the H
//              bars instead of the last close.
//    EXPOSURE  the instrument's own average risk ÷ risk now, capped, times a
//              trend throttle between a floor and 1. Changed only in steps.
//    LEDGER    nine states - trend down / flat / up × the surprise below /
//              inside / above the cone. For each, the next H bars' return in
//              σ, against this chart's own mean, shrunk toward "no edge". A
//              state is called PROVEN only past two posterior σ.
//
//  ═══ MEASURED (research/results.txt · the Python port is research/kasauti.py)
//    CALIBRATION   cone 80%: realised 80.0%; within 3 points of target in 99%
//                  of instrument-eras (a fixed normal band: 61%). Stops 20%:
//                  realised 20.0%, within 3 points in 99%. A 2 × ATR(14) stop
//                  is touched anywhere from 17% to 44% of the time depending
//                  on the instrument. Holds at H 5, 20 and 40, at 50% and 90%
//                  cones, on weekly bars and on hourly bars.
//    EXPOSURE      daily: Sharpe 0.55 against 0.53 for buy and hold, mean worst
//                  drawdown −44% against −62%, shallower on 99% of instruments
//                  or more in every era. After 2013 it does NOT beat buy and
//                  hold on Sharpe: it is risk control, not a return engine.
//                  Weekly: the same shape. HOURLY: IT LOST (0.26 against 0.42)
//                  - the dial is a daily and weekly tool.
//    LEDGER        pooled, no state reaches |t| = 1.3 outside crypto. On a daily
//                  chart almost every state will read UNPROVEN. That is the
//                  finding, not a fault.
//
//  WHAT IT WILL NOT DO. It does not call direction. The cone is a range, not
//  a target. Calibration is a long-run frequency: a cone can miss several
//  times in a row inside one shock. Stocks in the study are today's large
//  caps, which flatters buy and hold and the dial alike.
//
//  REPAINT POSTURE. The risk engine, cone, stops, tapes, dial and ledger are
//  computed from the chart's own bars. Values on the forming bar move until it
//  closes; history and realtime compute the same numbers. Alerts fire on closed
//  bars. The volume profile's developing session is the one disclosed
//  exception, as in Pragati.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
indicator("Kasauti · Calibrated Risk, Exposure and Self-Audit", shorttitle = "Kasauti", overlay = false,
     precision = 2, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 100, max_boxes_count = 500, max_polylines_count = 5)

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  INPUTS
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var string G_R = "1 · Risk forecast"
var string G_E = "2 · Exposure"
var string G_L = "3 · Ledger"
var string G_D = "4 · Display"

int    inpH     = input.int(10, "Horizon · H (bars)", minval = 4, maxval = 60, group = G_R, tooltip = "How far ahead every forecast looks. The cone is where the close should be H bars from now; a stop's probability is of being touched within H bars; the ledger scores the next H bars. The stretch ladder reads H/2, H, 2H and 4H.\n\nMeasured at 5, 10, 20 and 40: the cone and stops held their targets at each.")
float  inpCover = input.float(80.0, "Cone coverage (%)", minval = 50.0, maxval = 98.0, step = 5.0, group = G_R, tooltip = "The share of the time the close H bars ahead should land inside the cone. The remainder is split equally above and below.\n\nThe cone LEARNS its width until this is true on this chart - the table's calibration row shows how close it is. Measured at 50, 80 and 90.")
float  inpStop  = input.float(20.0, "Stop touch probability (%)", minval = 5.0, maxval = 50.0, step = 5.0, group = G_R, tooltip = "The long stop is the level price trades DOWN to within H bars this share of the time; the short stop mirrors it above.\n\nA tighter stop is touched more often. 20% means four holds in five reach the horizon untouched. Measured at 10, 20 and 30.")
float  inpEta   = input.float(0.02, "Calibration speed", minval = 0.005, maxval = 0.10, step = 0.005, group = G_R, tooltip = "How far one settled forecast moves the learned width. Higher adapts faster and holds its target more tightly, at the cost of a wider, jumpier cone.\n\nMeasured at 0.01, 0.02 and 0.05: all calibrate; 0.02 gave the narrowest cone that still held its target.")
bool   inpReg   = input.bool(true, "Cone listens to the RISK tape", group = G_R, tooltip = "Keep a separate learned width for calm, normal and stressed markets.\n\nMeasured: with one width for all, the cone held 80% overall but 76% in calm markets and 84% in stressed ones. Listening to the risk tape: 79%, 80% and 81%.")
bool   inpTrF   = input.bool(true, "Cone listens to the TREND tape", group = G_R, tooltip = "Add a learned term for trend down, flat and up, on each side separately - so the cone and the stops are skewed the way the instrument actually moves in each.\n\nMeasured: without it a short stop in a downtrend was touched 27% of the time against a stated 20%, and a long stop in an uptrend 22%. With it: 21% and 20%.")

string inpMode  = input.string("Risk × trend", "Exposure dial", options = ["Risk × trend", "Risk only"], group = G_E, tooltip = "RISK ONLY - the instrument's own average risk divided by its risk now, capped. Hold less when the instrument is wilder than usual.\n\nRISK × TREND (default) - the same, multiplied by a trend throttle between the floor and 1. Measured on daily bars: Sharpe about level with buy and hold, the worst drawdown about a quarter shallower, on 99% of instruments in every era. Insurance, with its premium stated.\n\nMeasured on HOURLY bars the dial LOST to buy and hold after costs. Use it on daily and weekly charts.")
float  inpCap   = input.float(1.0, "    Cap", minval = 0.25, maxval = 3.0, step = 0.25, group = G_E, tooltip = "The most the dial may read. 1.0 never levers: the dial only ever takes risk off.\n\nMeasured at 1.5 and 2.0: return rises with exposure but the drawdown advantage disappears.")
float  inpFloor = input.float(0.5, "    Trend floor", minval = 0.0, maxval = 1.0, step = 0.25, group = G_E, tooltip = "The least the trend throttle may cut to. 0.5: a full downtrend halves the position, never closes it.\n\nMeasured: 0.5 kept buy and hold's Sharpe; 0.25 and 0 gave shallower drawdowns still and lost Sharpe on most instruments.")
float  inpStep  = input.float(0.10, "    Step", minval = 0.0, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.05, group = G_E, tooltip = "The dial is acted on only when it has moved this far from the position held. 0 follows every wiggle.\n\nMeasured on daily bars: a step of 0.10 cut turnover by about two thirds and changed neither Sharpe nor drawdown.")
float  inpCost  = input.float(5.0, "    Cost (bp per unit of turnover)", minval = 0.0, maxval = 100.0, step = 1.0, group = G_E, tooltip = "Charged in the PROOF every time the position changes, on the size of the change. 5 bp is what the study used; 10 for crypto.")
float  inpRisk  = input.float(1.0, "Risk per trade (% of equity)", minval = 0.1, maxval = 10.0, step = 0.1, group = G_E, tooltip = "Used only for the table's size: the position, as a share of equity, that loses this much if the stop is touched.")

float  inpTau   = input.float(0.10, "Prior · how large an edge is believable (σ)", minval = 0.02, maxval = 0.50, step = 0.01, group = G_L, tooltip = "The ledger starts from the belief that a state has NO edge, and that a real one is of this size, in σ over H bars. Evidence has to overcome that belief before a state reads PROVEN.\n\n0.10 is generous: pooled across 151 instruments the largest state edge outside crypto was 0.06. On random walks the ledger then calls a state proven on 0.4% of bars.")
bool   inpMark  = input.bool(true, "Mark entries into a proven state", group = G_L, tooltip = "A small triangle on the price chart on the first bar of a state this chart's own history has proven - up for a positive edge, down for a negative one. Rare by design.")

string inpPane  = input.string("Surprise and tapes", "Pane", options = ["Surprise and tapes", "Proof"], group = G_D, tooltip = "SURPRISE AND TAPES - the realised H-bar move divided by the forecast made H bars ago, against the learned bands, between the four tapes.\n\nPROOF - cumulative growth, in log %, of following the dial against buy and hold on this chart: one bar late and net of the cost above.")
bool   inpTapes = input.bool(true, "Tapes", group = G_D, tooltip = "TREND and the STRETCH LADDER above the pane, RISK and RISK MOMENTUM below it. The two inner tapes are what the cone and the dial listen to; the two outer ones say where each is heading. Their readings are in the right-edge labels and the table.")
bool   inpCone  = input.bool(true, "Forward cone", group = G_D, tooltip = "The cone drawn from the last bar to H bars ahead, with the stops across it.")
bool   inpLand  = input.bool(true, "Landing band", group = G_D, tooltip = "The cone that was drawn H bars ago, plotted at each bar. A close outside it is a surprise.")
bool   inpTrail = input.bool(false, "Stop history", group = G_D, tooltip = "Draws where the long and short stops stood on every past bar. Off by default: the current stops are always drawn across the forward cone and listed in the table.")
bool   inpTbl   = input.bool(true, "Table", group = G_D)
string inpPos   = input.string("Bottom left", "    Position", options = ["Bottom left", "Top left", "Bottom right", "Top right"], group = G_D, tooltip = "On the price chart. Bottom left is the corner the volume profile and its tag column do not claim.")
string inpTheme = input.string("Auto", "Palette", options = ["Auto", "Light", "Dark"], group = G_D)

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  PALETTE
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
float bgLum    = color.r(chart.bg_color) * 0.299 + color.g(chart.bg_color) * 0.587 + color.b(chart.bg_color) * 0.114
bool  darkMode = inpTheme == "Dark" or (inpTheme == "Auto" and bgLum < 128)
color C_UP    = darkMode ? #3FB980 : #08724A
color C_DN    = darkMode ? #E4776A : #A8443A
color C_NEUT  = darkMode ? #8A97A0 : #69757E
color C_CONE  = darkMode ? #5B8FD6 : #2C5C99
color C_GOLD  = darkMode ? #D9B44A : #8A6A0E               // risk - never a direction
color C_TEXT  = darkMode ? #C9D1D6 : #2B3338
color C_PANEL = darkMode ? color.new(#0D1215, 8) : color.new(#FFFFFF, 6)

// profile palette — PVOI's, as in Pragati
color C_POC    = darkMode ? #FFB020 : #B26A00      // point of control — warm anchor
color C_VA     = darkMode ? #5B8FD6 : #2C5C99      // value-area boundaries + band, cool
color C_VWAP   = darkMode ? #F06BA8 : #A32468      // volume-weighted average, rose
color C_NODE   = darkMode ? #6E7C88 : #8A949B      // monochrome out-of-value tails · neutral grey
color C_HVN    = darkMode ? #8F7BD8 : #5E4B9E      // High-Volume Node · dense violet
color C_LVN    = darkMode ? #C6BBEA : #8F7DBB      // Low-Volume Node  · pale  violet
color C_VIOLET = darkMode ? #A87ABF : #6A3F84      // Initial Balance

// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  HELPERS
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_tanh(float x) =>
    float xc = math.max(-10.0, math.min(10.0, x))
    float e  = math.exp(2.0 * xc)
    (e - 1.0) / (e + 1.0)

// Inverse normal CDF (Acklam), accurate to 2e-9. Used once, to start the
// learned widths where a normal distribution would put them.
f_invTail(float q) =>
    (((((-7.784894002430293e-03 * q - 3.223964580411365e-01) * q - 2.400758277161838) * q - 2.549732539343734) * q + 4.374664141464968) * q + 2.938163982698783) /
     ((((7.784695709041462e-03 * q + 3.224671290700398e-01) * q + 2.445134137142996) * q + 3.754408661907416) * q + 1.0)
f_invNorm(float p) =>
    float x = 0.0
    if p < 0.02425
        x := f_invTail(math.sqrt(-2.0 * math.log(p)))
    else if p > 1.0 - 0.02425
        x := -f_invTail(math.sqrt(-2.0 * math.log(1.0 - p)))
    else
        float q = p - 0.5
        float r = q * q
        x := (((((-3.969683028665376e+01 * r + 2.209460984245205e+02) * r - 2.759285104469687e+02) * r + 1.383577518672690e+02) * r - 3.066479806614716e+01) * r + 2.506628277459239) * q /
             (((((-5.447609879822406e+01 * r + 1.615858368580409e+02) * r - 1.556989798598866e+02) * r + 6.680131188771972e+01) * r - 1.328068155288572e+01) * r + 1.0)
    x

f_pct(float x, string fmt) => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(100.0 * x, fmt) + "%"
f_num(float x, string fmt) => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, fmt)
f_px(float x)              => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, format.mintick)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  1 · THE RISK FORECAST
//
//  One bar's variance from its whole range and its gap (Garman-Klass), which
//  uses about five times the information of a squared close-to-close return.
//  Three horizons blended with fixed weights, then rescaled so the level
//  matches close-to-close variance on this instrument. The weights are round
//  numbers near a fit on 2001-2012 and beat that fit on 2013-2026.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
const int WARM = 252
const int RN   = 500

float lc = math.log(close)
float lnO = math.log(open)
float r1 = lc - lc[1]
float gp = lnO - lc[1]
float co = lc - lnO
float hl = math.log(high) - math.log(low)
float gk = gp * gp + 0.5 * hl * hl - (2.0 * math.log(2.0) - 1.0) * co * co
float vBar  = hl > 0.0 and gk > 0.0 ? gk : r1 * r1            // a bar with no range falls back to its squared return
float varS = ta.ema(vBar, 5)
float varM = ta.ema(vBar, 22)
float varL = ta.ema(vBar, 252)
float rL = ta.ema(r1 * r1, 252)
float kk = varL > 0.0 ? math.max(0.5, math.min(2.0, rL / varL)) : 1.0
float s0 = bar_index >= WARM ? math.sqrt(kk * (0.25 * varS + 0.40 * varM + 0.35 * varL)) : na
float sig = s0 > 0.0 ? s0 : na                              // risk per bar, in log return
float sH  = sig * math.sqrt(inpH)                           // risk over the horizon

// THE RISK TAPE: where this bar's risk stands among the last RN bars.
float prk    = ta.percentrank(sig, RN)
bool  regOk  = bar_index >= WARM + RN and not na(prk)
int   regRaw = regOk ? (prk < 100.0 / 3.0 ? 0 : prk < 200.0 / 3.0 ? 1 : 2) : 1
int   reg    = inpReg ? regRaw : 1                          // the regime the cone listens to

// RISK MOMENTUM: the change in forecast risk over the last H bars.
float rMom = math.log(sig / sig[inpH])
int   rmS  = rMom > 0.10 ? 2 : rMom < -0.10 ? 0 : 1

// THE TREND TAPE, in σ: the move over a quarter, a half and a whole year of
// bars, each divided by what today's risk says such a move should be.
float T = ((lc - lc[63]) / (sig * math.sqrt(63.0)) + (lc - lc[126]) / (sig * math.sqrt(126.0)) + (lc - lc[252]) / (sig * math.sqrt(252.0))) / 3.0
int trRaw = T > 0.5 ? 2 : T < -0.5 ? 0 : 1
int trs   = inpTrF ? trRaw : 1                              // the trend state the cone listens to

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  2 · THE CONE, THE STOPS AND THE LADDER · LEARNED WIDTHS
//
//  Each bar settles the forecast made h bars ago: where the close landed, in
//  units of that forecast's own σ. Each width then moves in logs by
//
//      log q ← log q + η · ( miss − target )
//
//  so it rises on a miss and falls on a hit in exactly the ratio at which the
//  miss rate equals the target. log q is the sum of a term for the risk regime
//  and a term for the trend state the forecast was made in, and both terms
//  take the step - so the target is met in every regime and in every trend
//  state, with six numbers a side instead of nine. No distribution is assumed.
//
//  A width array holds six numbers: [0..2] by risk regime, [3..5] by trend.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float aTail = (1.0 - inpCover / 100.0) / 2.0
float pTch  = inpStop / 100.0
float zInit = math.log(f_invNorm(1.0 - aTail))
float sInit = math.log(f_invNorm(1.0 - pTch / 2.0))         // a Brownian path touches −b with probability 2·Φ(−b)

f_new(float b0) =>
    array<float> a = array.new_float(6, 0.0)
    array.set(a, 0, b0)
    array.set(a, 1, b0)
    array.set(a, 2, b0)
    a
f_q(array<float> a, int rg, int tr) => math.exp(array.get(a, rg) + array.get(a, 3 + tr))
f_step(array<float> a, int rg, int tr, float e) =>
    array.set(a, rg, array.get(a, rg) + e)
    array.set(a, 3 + tr, array.get(a, 3 + tr) + (inpTrF ? e : 0.0))

// One rung of the horizon ladder. Returns the surprise, the band it is judged
// against (the one in force when its forecast was made), whether it broke
// either side, whether it has settled, the surprise as a fraction of its band,
// and the widths now in force.
f_rung(simple int h, array<float> wU, array<float> wD) =>
    float qu  = na
    float qd  = na
    float uu  = (lc - lc[h]) / (sig[h] * math.sqrt(h))
    float quP = qu[h]
    float qdP = qd[h]
    int   rgP = reg[h]
    int   trP = trs[h]
    bool  ok  = not na(uu) and not na(quP)
    bool  up  = ok and uu >  quP
    bool  dn  = ok and uu < -qdP
    if ok
        f_step(wU, rgP, trP, inpEta * ((up ? 1.0 : 0.0) - aTail))
        f_step(wD, rgP, trP, inpEta * ((dn ? 1.0 : 0.0) - aTail))
    if not na(sig)
        qu := f_q(wU, reg, trs)
        qd := f_q(wD, reg, trs)
    float x = not ok ? na : uu >= 0.0 ? uu / quP : uu / qdP
    [uu, quP, qdP, up, dn, ok, x, qu, qd]

int h0 = math.max(2, int(math.floor(inpH / 2)))
int h2 = 2 * inpH
int h3 = 4 * inpH

var array<float> wU0 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD0 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU1 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD1 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU2 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD2 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wU3 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wD3 = f_new(zInit)
var array<float> wS  = f_new(sInit)                         // long stop
var array<float> wR  = f_new(sInit)                         // short stop

[u0, bU0, bD0, up0, dn0, ok0, lx0, qU0, qD0] = f_rung(h0,   wU0, wD0)
[u,  bU,  bD,  mU,  mD,  settled, lx1, qU, qD] = f_rung(inpH, wU1, wD1)     // the pane's own rung
[u2, bU2, bD2, up2, dn2, ok2, lx2, qU2, qD2] = f_rung(h2,   wU2, wD2)
[u3, bU3, bD3, up3, dn3, ok3, lx3, qU3, qD3] = f_rung(h3,   wU3, wD3)

// THE STRETCH LADDER: how many rungs are outside their own cone, and its mean
// position as a fraction of the bands.
bool  ladOk  = ok0 and settled and ok2 and ok3
int   ladUp  = (up0 ? 1 : 0) + (mU ? 1 : 0) + (up2 ? 1 : 0) + (up3 ? 1 : 0)
int   ladDn  = (dn0 ? 1 : 0) + (mD ? 1 : 0) + (dn2 ? 1 : 0) + (dn3 ? 1 : 0)
float ladX   = ladOk ? (lx0 + lx1 + lx2 + lx3) / 4.0 : na
int   ladN   = ladX >= 0.0 ? ladUp : ladDn                  // rungs outside on the side it leans

// The stops: settled on the path, not the close.
float qS = na
float qR = na
float pS = (math.log(ta.lowest(low, inpH))   - lc[inpH]) / sH[inpH]
float pR = (math.log(ta.highest(high, inpH)) - lc[inpH]) / sH[inpH]
float qSP = qS[inpH]
float qRP = qR[inpH]
int   regPrev = reg[inpH]
int   trPrev  = trs[inpH]
bool  mS = settled and pS < -qSP                            // the long stop was touched
bool  mR = settled and pR >  qRP                            // the short stop was touched

var int nF  = 0
var int nMU = 0
var int nMD = 0
var int nMS = 0
var int nMR = 0

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  3 · THE LEDGER
//
//  Nine states. For each, every bar spent in it is scored H bars later by the
//  return from the NEXT bar's open to that close, in the forecast's σ, clipped
//  at ±6 so one bad print cannot own a state. Samples are counted as
//  independent only when their signal bars are at least H apart.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var array<float> lCnt  = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<float> lMean = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<float> lEff  = array.new_float(9, 0.0)
var array<int>   lLast = array.new_int(9, -1000000000)
var int   gN = 0
var float gM = 0.0
var float gQ = 0.0

int   st     = -1
float yRaw   = (lc - lnO[inpH - 1]) / sH[inpH]
float yOut      = na(yRaw) ? na : math.max(-6.0, math.min(6.0, yRaw))
int   stPrev = st[inpH]

if settled
    f_step(wS, regPrev, trPrev, inpEta * ((mS ? 1.0 : 0.0) - pTch))
    f_step(wR, regPrev, trPrev, inpEta * ((mR ? 1.0 : 0.0) - pTch))
    nF  += 1
    nMU += mU ? 1 : 0
    nMD += mD ? 1 : 0
    nMS += mS ? 1 : 0
    nMR += mR ? 1 : 0
    if stPrev >= 0 and not na(yOut)
        float c1 = array.get(lCnt, stPrev) + 1.0
        array.set(lCnt, stPrev, c1)
        array.set(lMean, stPrev, array.get(lMean, stPrev) + (yOut - array.get(lMean, stPrev)) / c1)
        gN += 1
        if bar_index - inpH - array.get(lLast, stPrev) >= inpH
            array.set(lEff, stPrev, array.get(lEff, stPrev) + 1.0)
            array.set(lLast, stPrev, bar_index - inpH)
        float dlt = yOut - gM
        gM += dlt / gN
        gQ += dlt * (yOut - gM)

if not na(sig)
    qS := f_q(wS, reg, trs)
    qR := f_q(wR, reg, trs)

int cnS = mU ? 2 : mD ? 0 : 1
if settled and not na(T)
    st := 3 * trRaw + cnS

// This state's record so far, against the chart's own mean, shrunk toward zero.
float lEdge = na
float lPost = na
float lZ    = na
float lNe   = st >= 0 ? array.get(lEff, st) : na
float lMu   = st >= 0 ? array.get(lMean, st) : na
if st >= 0 and lNe >= 5.0 and gN > 30 * inpH
    float se2 = gQ / (gN - 1) / lNe
    float shr = inpTau * inpTau / (inpTau * inpTau + se2)
    lEdge := lMu - gM
    lPost := shr * lEdge
    lZ    := lEdge * math.sqrt(shr / se2)
int  proven   = lZ >= 2.0 ? 1 : lZ <= -2.0 ? -1 : 0
bool stEnter  = st >= 0 and st != st[1]
bool provenUp = barstate.isconfirmed and stEnter and proven ==  1
bool provenDn = barstate.isconfirmed and stEnter and proven == -1

// Calibration over the last 250 settled forecasts - the recent record.
float covRecent = 1.0 - ta.sma(settled ? (mU or mD ? 1.0 : 0.0) : na, 250)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  4 · LEVELS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float upper = close * math.exp( qU * sH)
float lower = close * math.exp(-qD * sH)
float stopL = close * math.exp(-qS * sH)
float stopS = close * math.exp( qR * sH)
bool  coneOk = not na(sig) and not na(qU) and not na(qS)

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  5 · THE EXPOSURE DIAL
//
//  The instrument's own average risk so far, over its risk now: one when the
//  instrument is as wild as it usually is, less when it is wilder. The trend
//  throttle runs from the floor in a full downtrend to 1 in a full uptrend.
//  The position HELD follows the dial only in steps.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float sumSig = 0.0
var int   nSig   = 0
if not na(sig)
    sumSig += sig
    nSig   += 1
float sigStar = nSig > 0 ? sumSig / nSig : na
float dialR   = na(sig) ? na : math.min(inpCap, sigStar / sig)
float dialT   = inpMode == "Risk only" ? 1.0 : na(T) ? na : inpFloor + (1.0 - inpFloor) * (0.5 + 0.5 * f_tanh(T))
float dial    = na(T) ? na : dialR * dialT

var float held = na
if not na(dial) and (na(held) or math.abs(dial - held) >= inpStep)
    held := dial
float E = na(dial) ? na : held

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  6 · THE PROOF
//
//  The position held at the close of bar t−2 is the position over bar t: one
//  full bar to act on it. Costs are charged on every change. Buy and hold is
//  scored over the same bars.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
float ret = close / close[1] - 1.0
float e2  = E[2]
float e3  = E[3]
float pF  = na(e2) ? na : e2 * ret - inpCost / 10000.0 * math.abs(e2 - nz(e3, 0.0))
float pH  = na(e2) ? na : ret

var int   nP   = 0
var int   tP   = na
var float sF   = 0.0
var float sF2  = 0.0
var float sHd  = 0.0
var float sHd2 = 0.0
var float eqF  = 1.0
var float eqH  = 1.0
var float pkF  = 1.0
var float pkH  = 1.0
var float ddF  = 0.0
var float ddH  = 0.0
if not na(pF) and not na(pH)
    if na(tP)
        tP := time
    nP   += 1
    sF   += pF
    sF2  += pF * pF
    sHd  += pH
    sHd2 += pH * pH
    eqF  *= 1.0 + pF
    eqH  *= 1.0 + pH
    pkF  := math.max(pkF, eqF)
    pkH  := math.max(pkH, eqH)
    ddF  := math.min(ddF, eqF / pkF - 1.0)
    ddH  := math.min(ddH, eqH / pkH - 1.0)

float yrs   = na(tP) ? na : (time - tP) / 31557600000.0
float bpy   = yrs > 0.0 ? nP / yrs : na                     // bars per year, measured on this chart
float sdF   = nP > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max(sF2 / nP - math.pow(sF / nP, 2), 0.0)) : na
float sdHd  = nP > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max(sHd2 / nP - math.pow(sHd / nP, 2), 0.0)) : na
float shF   = sdF  > 0.0 ? sF  / nP / sdF  * math.sqrt(bpy) : na
float shH   = sdHd > 0.0 ? sHd / nP / sdHd * math.sqrt(bpy) : na
float cagF  = yrs > 0.0 and eqF > 0.0 ? math.pow(eqF, 1.0 / yrs) - 1.0 : na
float cagH  = yrs > 0.0 and eqH > 0.0 ? math.pow(eqH, 1.0 / yrs) - 1.0 : na

// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  7 · VOLUME PROFILE · MARKET-STRUCTURE OVERLAY       (Pragati's, from PVOI v2.1)
//  ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  A PRICE-CHART overlay: session volume profile (histogram + POC/VAH/VAL value
//  area), plus session VWAP, Initial Balance, naked POCs, HVN/LVN nodes,
//  prior-session levels and developing-level trails. Kasauti is a pane script,
//  so every element is drawn with force_overlay = true.
//
//  DISPLAY-ONLY AND FULLY DETACHED. It touches NOTHING - not the risk forecast,
//  the cone, the stops, the dial or the ledger. Everything is namespaced
//  vp*/C_* so it cannot collide with the engine's own state. Removing this
//  whole block leaves Kasauti intact.
//
//  CARRIED IN WHOLE from Pragati, line for line, with three changes only:
//    · the profile sits to the RIGHT of the forward cone;
//    · the stops' and the cone's tags are seated in its tag column, first,
//      under its collision control;
//    · the gates read this script's switches, and green / red are this
//      script's C_UP / C_DN.
//
//  Sorted-key bins, O(1) POC, value-area walk outward from the POC, optional
//  intrabar distribution and inferred buy/sell delta. Session anchor = D intraday,
//  W on daily, M above. request.security_lower_tf history depth is plan-dependent;
//  the profile falls back to a uniform bar-range spread when it is unavailable.
// ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var string G_VP = "5 · Volume profile · price chart"
bool   inpVpMaster    = input.bool(true,  "Volume profile", group=G_VP, tooltip="ON by default. The master switch: off removes every chart-overlay element below AND stops the profile being computed — the accumulation loop, the row inserts, the value-area walk and the naked-POC ledger all stand down, so this is a real off switch rather than a curtain over work that keeps running. The profile is also skipped, on its own, whenever every layer that draws from it is off (VWAP and Initial Balance do not need it).\n\nThe pane is unaffected either way; nothing in the risk engine reads the profile.\n\nONE COST CANNOT BE SWITCHED OFF: Pine requires request.security_lower_tf() at global scope, so the lower-timeframe fetch happens whether or not the profile uses it. Nothing else does.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpIntrabar  = input.bool(true,  "    Build from intrabar data", group=G_VP, tooltip="request.security_lower_tf() distributes volume by ACTUAL traded price. More accurate, slower, plan-dependent history. Falls back automatically.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpUseVol    = input.bool(true,  "    Volume-weighted", group=G_VP, tooltip="Off degrades the profile to a time-at-price (TPO) distribution — for spot FX / synthetic volume.", display=display.none)
string inpVpBinMode   = input.string("ATR adaptive", "    Bin grid", options=["ATR adaptive", "Fixed ticks"], group=G_VP, display=display.none)
float  inpVpBinsPerAtr= input.float(4.0,  "        Bins per ATR · ATR mode", minval=1.0, maxval=20.0, step=0.5, group=G_VP, tooltip="Bin width = ATR / this. Frozen at session start so keys stay consistent within a profile.", display=display.none)
int    inpVpBinTicks  = input.int(20,     "        Bin size (ticks) · fixed mode", minval=1, maxval=5000, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
float  inpVpVaPct     = input.float(0.70, "    Value area fraction", minval=0.50, maxval=0.95, step=0.01, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpHistg     = input.bool(true,  "    Histogram", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
string inpVpStyle     = input.string("Monochrome", "        Histogram style", options=["Monochrome", "Delta split"], group=G_VP, tooltip="MONOCHROME (default): one box per row, amber POC row inside blue value-area rows, grey out-of-value tails. Hue marks identity only, never direction.\n\nDELTA SPLIT: each row divides into green (inferred buy) and red (inferred sell) volume; the POC row is an amber outline. The buy/sell split is inferred, not measured order flow, and is computed only for this style.", display=display.none)
bool   vpMono         = inpVpStyle == "Monochrome"
bool   inpVpDelta     = not vpMono     // the buy/sell split is computed only when drawn
int    inpVpWidth     = input.int(30,     "        Histogram width (bars)", minval=8, maxval=150, group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpNodes     = input.bool(true,  "        HVN / LVN markers", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpVa        = input.bool(true,  "    Value area (VAH / VAL)", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpPoc       = input.bool(true,  "    POC line", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpTrail     = input.bool(true,  "    Developing level trails", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpPrev      = input.bool(true,  "    Prior session value", group=G_VP, tooltip="Last session's pPOC, pVAH and pVAL — three dotted lines, drawn only across the session in front of you. These are the reference the market is currently accepting or rejecting, which is why they are not stacked back through history.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpNaked     = input.bool(true,  "    Naked POC (untouched)", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
int    inpVpNakedMax  = input.int(5,      "        Naked POC · max kept", minval=1, maxval=20, group=G_VP, tooltip="How many untouched POCs the ledger carries. The oldest is dropped when the ledger is full.\n\nThe original ceiling was twelve, and on a long chart twelve amber dotted lines stop being a reference and become the chart. A level you cannot count is not a level. Five is enough to see the unfinished business above and below without burying the price action; raise it only if you are actually trading to the older ones.", display=display.none)
int    inpVpNakedAge  = input.int(250,    "        Naked POC · max age (bars)", minval=50, maxval=1000, step=25, group=G_VP, tooltip="A naked POC older than this is dropped whether or not price ever traded through it, and no line starts further back than this. A point of control from four hundred bars ago describes a market that no longer exists.", display=display.none)
bool   inpVpVwap      = input.bool(true,  "    Session VWAP", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
bool   inpVpIb        = input.bool(true,  "    Initial Balance (IBH / IBL)", group=G_VP, display=display.none)
int    inpVpIbBars    = input.int(12,     "        Initial Balance span (bars)", minval=3, maxval=60, group=G_VP, display=display.none)

// ── gates, resolved once ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bool   vpChartOn  = inpVpMaster
// THE MASTER NOW GATES COMPUTE AS WELL AS DRAWING. Before this it only silenced
// the chart objects while the accumulation loop, the row inserts and the value-
// area walk all still ran on every bar. A switch that turns the picture off and
// leaves the work on is not an off switch.
// the profile is built only when a layer drawn from it is on. VWAP and IB do not need it.
bool   vpCtxOn    = vpChartOn and (inpVpHistg or inpVpVa or inpVpPoc or inpVpTrail or inpVpPrev or inpVpNaked)
bool   vpIsIntra  = timeframe.isintraday
int    vpTfSec    = timeframe.in_seconds()
// AUTO-TPO FALLBACK. On a symbol reporting no volume every row received zero, so
// pocVol never exceeded zero and the `pocVol > 0` guard suppressed the histogram,
// the POC and the value area entirely - the profile simply did not appear, with
// nothing to explain why, and the panel still read "Volume" because it reported the
// user's INTENT rather than what happened. Index spot and most TVC symbols are
// exactly that case. The share of bars carrying real volume decides it now.
float  vpVolShare = ta.cum((na(volume) or volume == 0.0) ? 0.0 : 1.0) / (bar_index + 1)
bool   vpVolUsable= vpVolShare >= 0.5
bool   vpVolOff   = not inpVpUseVol or not vpVolUsable
bool   vpVolOk    = not vpVolOff          // what ACTUALLY happened, not what was asked
bool   vpTpoAuto  = inpVpUseVol and not vpVolUsable
string vpAnchorTf = vpIsIntra ? "D" : timeframe.isdaily ? "W" : "M"
// The first bar opens a session too. Without it the first partial session had no
// frozen bin width and no session start, so it drew no profile and its Initial
// Balance stretched across the whole of it. The flip is evaluated on its own line
// first so ta.change runs on every bar under v6's lazy `or`.
bool   vpSessFlip = ta.change(time(vpAnchorTf)) != 0
bool   vpNewSess  = barstate.isfirst or vpSessFlip
bool   vpHistOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpHistg and vpCtxOn
bool   vpVaOn     = vpChartOn and inpVpVa    and vpCtxOn
bool   vpPocOn    = vpChartOn and inpVpPoc   and vpCtxOn
bool   vpNodesOn  = vpHistOn  and inpVpNodes
bool   vpNakedOn  = vpChartOn and inpVpNaked and vpCtxOn
bool   vpPrevOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpPrev  and vpCtxOn
bool   vpTrailOn  = vpChartOn and inpVpTrail and vpCtxOn
bool   vpVwapOn   = vpChartOn and inpVpVwap
bool   vpIbOn     = vpChartOn and inpVpIb

// ATR floor. Floored to mintick so the session-start bin freeze never freezes to
// na and blanks the first session. ta.* must be evaluated on EVERY bar, never
// inside the session branch that consumes it.
float vpATR = math.max(nz(ta.atr(20), syminfo.mintick), syminfo.mintick)

// ── helpers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
f_vpLocate(array<int> keys, int k) =>
    int  lo    = 0
    int  hi    = array.size(keys) - 1
    int  pos   = 0
    bool found = false
    while lo <= hi
        int mid = (lo + hi) / 2
        int mk  = array.get(keys, mid)
        if mk == k
            pos   := mid
            found := true
            break
        else if mk < k
            lo := mid + 1
        else
            hi := mid - 1
    if not found
        pos := lo
    [pos, found]

f_vpAdd(array<int> keys, array<float> vols, array<float> buys, array<float> sells, int k, float v, float bv, float sv) =>
    [pos, found] = f_vpLocate(keys, k)
    float nv = v
    if found
        nv := array.get(vols, pos) + v
        array.set(vols,  pos, nv)
        array.set(buys,  pos, array.get(buys,  pos) + bv)
        array.set(sells, pos, array.get(sells, pos) + sv)
    else
        array.insert(keys,  pos, k)
        array.insert(vols,  pos, v)
        array.insert(buys,  pos, bv)
        array.insert(sells, pos, sv)
    nv

// ── profile state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
var array<int>   vpKey  = array.new<int>()
var array<float> vpVol  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> vpBuy  = array.new<float>()
var array<float> vpSell = array.new<float>()
var float vpBin   = na
var float vpTotal = 0.0
var int   pocKey  = na
var float pocVol  = 0.0
var float poc     = na
var float vah     = na
var float vaLow   = na
var float prevPoc = na
var float prevVah = na
var float prevVal = na
var bool  vpIntraOk = false

// intrabar distribution (falls back automatically when unavailable)
// On a chart at or below one minute there is no lower timeframe worth spreading
// by, and on a SECONDS chart "1" is HIGHER than the chart - a runtime error. The
// request then asks for the chart's own timeframe (harmless) and intrabar
// distribution stands down.
string vpLtf      = vpTfSec >= 3600 ? "5" : vpTfSec > 60 ? "1" : timeframe.period
bool   vpIntraUse = inpVpIntrabar and vpTfSec > 60
[vpIbHi, vpIbLo, vpIbVol, vpIbClose] = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, vpLtf, [high, low, volume, close])

// inferred delta (DISPLAY ONLY) — gap-aware close-location share to buyers
float vpTrHi  = math.max(high, nz(close[1], high))
float vpTrLo  = math.min(low,  nz(close[1], low))
float vpTrRng = math.max(vpTrHi - vpTrLo, syminfo.mintick)
float vpShare = inpVpDelta ? math.min(1.0, math.max(0.0, (close - vpTrLo) / vpTrRng)) : 0.5
float vpBarV  = vpVolOff ? 1.0 : math.max(nz(volume), 0.0)
float vpBarB  = vpBarV * vpShare
float vpBarS  = vpBarV - vpBarB

// The profile's accumulation and value-area walk, as a function: its loops
// sit outside the script's main body, whose length Pine caps. The four bin
// arrays are references; the state it changes comes back.
float vpC1 = close[1]
f_vpBuild(float tot0, int key0, float vol0, bool used0, float poc0, float vah0, float val0) =>
    float sTot  = tot0
    int   sKey  = key0
    float sVol  = vol0
    bool  sUsed = used0
    float sPoc  = poc0
    float sVah  = vah0
    float sVal  = val0
    if not na(vpBin) and vpBin > 0
        bool usedIntrabar = false
        if vpIntraUse and not na(vpIbHi) and not na(vpIbLo) and not na(vpIbVol) and not na(vpIbClose)
            int m = array.size(vpIbHi)
            if m > 0 and m == array.size(vpIbLo) and m == array.size(vpIbVol) and m == array.size(vpIbClose)
                usedIntrabar := true
                float prevC = vpC1
                for j = 0 to m - 1
                    float ih = array.get(vpIbHi, j)
                    float il = array.get(vpIbLo,  j)
                    // TPO: each CHART bar is one unit of time, split across its
                    // intrabars - otherwise an intrabar-built bar counted m times
                    // what a fallback bar counted in the same session.
                    float iv = vpVolOff ? 1.0 / m : math.max(nz(array.get(vpIbVol, j)), 0.0)
                    float ic = array.get(vpIbClose, j)
                    float bvn = iv * 0.5
                    float svn = iv * 0.5
                    if inpVpDelta and not na(ic) and not na(prevC)
                        if ic > prevC
                            bvn := iv
                            svn := 0.0
                        else if ic < prevC
                            bvn := 0.0
                            svn := iv
                    if not na(ic)
                        prevC := ic
                    if not na(ih) and not na(il)
                        int kl = int(math.floor(il / vpBin))
                        int kh = int(math.floor(ih / vpBin))
                        int nb = math.max(1, math.min(kh - kl + 1, 200))
                        float per  = iv  / nb
                        float perB = bvn / nb
                        float perS = svn / nb
                        for k = kl to kl + nb - 1
                            float tot = f_vpAdd(vpKey, vpVol, vpBuy, vpSell, k, per, perB, perS)
                            sTot += per
                            if tot > sVol
                                sVol := tot
                                sKey := k
        if not usedIntrabar
            int kl = int(math.floor(low  / vpBin))
            int kh = int(math.floor(high / vpBin))
            int nb = math.max(1, math.min(kh - kl + 1, 200))
            float per  = vpBarV / nb
            float perB = vpBarB / nb
            float perS = vpBarS / nb
            for k = kl to kl + nb - 1
                float tot = f_vpAdd(vpKey, vpVol, vpBuy, vpSell, k, per, perB, perS)
                sTot += per
                if tot > sVol
                    sVol := tot
                    sKey := k

        sUsed := usedIntrabar

    int nLev = array.size(vpKey)
    if nLev > 0 and not na(sKey) and not na(vpBin)
        [pi, pfound] = f_vpLocate(vpKey, sKey)
        if pfound
            float target = sTot * inpVpVaPct
            int   lo    = pi
            int   hi    = pi
            float acc   = array.get(vpVol, pi)
            int   guard = 0
            while acc < target and (lo > 0 or hi < nLev - 1) and guard < nLev + 2
                guard += 1
                float vd = lo > 0        ? array.get(vpVol, lo - 1) : -1.0
                float vu = hi < nLev - 1 ? array.get(vpVol, hi + 1) : -1.0
                if vu >= vd
                    hi  += 1
                    acc += vu
                else
                    lo  -= 1
                    acc += vd
            sPoc := (sKey + 0.5) * vpBin
            sVah := (array.get(vpKey, hi) + 1.0) * vpBin
            sVal := array.get(vpKey, lo) * vpBin
    [sTot, sKey, sVol, sUsed, sPoc, sVah, sVal]

if vpCtxOn
    if vpNewSess
        prevPoc := poc
        prevVah := vah
        prevVal := vaLow
        array.clear(vpKey)
        array.clear(vpVol)
        array.clear(vpBuy)
        array.clear(vpSell)
        vpTotal := 0.0
        pocKey  := na
        pocVol  := 0.0
        vpBin   := inpVpBinMode == "Fixed ticks" ? math.max(syminfo.mintick, inpVpBinTicks * syminfo.mintick) : math.max(syminfo.mintick, vpATR / inpVpBinsPerAtr)
    [bTot, bKey, bVol, bUsed, bPoc, bVah, bVal] = f_vpBuild(vpTotal, pocKey, pocVol, vpIntraOk, poc, vah, vaLow)
    vpTotal   := bTot
    pocKey    := bKey
    pocVol    := bVol
    vpIntraOk := bUsed
    poc       := bPoc
    vah       := bVah
    vaLow     := bVal

// ── naked POC ledger (measured) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
//  Capped by input rather than at a hard twelve: twelve amber dotted lines on a
//  long chart stop being a reference and become the chart.
var array<float> vpNpY = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   vpNpX = array.new<int>()
if barstate.isconfirmed and array.size(vpNpY) > 0
    int kn = array.size(vpNpY) - 1
    while kn >= 0
        if high >= array.get(vpNpY, kn) and low <= array.get(vpNpY, kn)
            array.remove(vpNpY, kn)
            array.remove(vpNpX, kn)
        kn -= 1
if vpCtxOn and vpNewSess and not na(prevPoc)
    bool dupN = false
    if array.size(vpNpY) > 0
        for qn = 0 to array.size(vpNpY) - 1
            if math.abs(array.get(vpNpY, qn) - prevPoc) <= vpATR * 0.1
                dupN := true
                break
    if not dupN
        array.push(vpNpY, prevPoc)
        array.push(vpNpX, bar_index)
        while array.size(vpNpY) > inpVpNakedMax
            array.shift(vpNpY)
            array.shift(vpNpX)
while array.size(vpNpX) > 0
    if bar_index - array.get(vpNpX, 0) > inpVpNakedAge
        array.shift(vpNpY)
        array.shift(vpNpX)
    else
        break

// ── session VWAP + Initial Balance (measured) ─────────────────────────────────
var float vpSessPv = 0.0
var float vpSessVv = 0.0
var float vpIbh    = na
var float vpIbl    = na
var int   vpSessStart = na
if vpChartOn
    if vpNewSess
        vpSessPv    := 0.0
        vpSessVv    := 0.0
        vpIbh       := high
        vpIbl       := low
        vpSessStart := bar_index
    float wV = vpVolOff ? 1.0 : math.max(nz(volume), 1e-10)
    vpSessPv += hlc3 * wV
    vpSessVv += wV
    if bar_index - nz(vpSessStart, bar_index) < inpVpIbBars       // bars 0 … n-1 = n bars
        vpIbh := math.max(nz(vpIbh, high), high)
        vpIbl := math.min(nz(vpIbl, low), low)
float vpVwap = vpSessVv > 0 ? vpSessPv / vpSessVv : na

// ── right-edge tag column + collision control ─────────────────────────────────
int VP_GUTTER = 4
int VP_XBACK  = 5000          // furthest-back x any profile drawing may take
int VP_OFFSET = 3             // extra bars of air between the last candle and the profile
int VP_CONE   = inpCone ? inpH : 0                          // the forward cone's bars: the profile sits to its right
int vpLeft    = bar_index + VP_CONE + 3 + VP_OFFSET
int vpRight   = vpLeft + inpVpWidth
var int tagX  = 0
var array<float> tagRows = array.new<float>()

f_rowFree(float y) =>
    float minGap = vpATR * 0.30
    bool  free   = true
    if array.size(tagRows) > 0
        for yy in tagRows
            if math.abs(yy - y) < minGap
                free := false
                break
    free

f_vpTag(label lb, float y, string txt, color col, bool on) =>
    label.delete(lb)
    bool draw = on and not na(y) and f_rowFree(y)
    if draw
        array.push(tagRows, y)
    draw ? label.new(tagX, y, txt + "  " + str.tostring(y, format.mintick),
              xloc.bar_index, yloc.price, color.new(col, 88), label.style_label_left,
              col, size.tiny, force_overlay = true) : label(na)

// ── developing-level trails + VWAP curve (force_overlay) ──────────────────────
// Blank on the session-open bar so yesterday's finals never connect to today.
// force_overlay relocates these to the MAIN chart pane, so they render as price-
// level curves and never touch the pane's own scale.
plot(vpTrailOn and vpVaOn  and not vpNewSess ? vah   : na, "VP · VAH trail", color.new(C_VA, 75), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.price_scale)
plot(vpTrailOn and vpVaOn  and not vpNewSess ? vaLow : na, "VP · VAL trail", color.new(C_VA, 75), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.price_scale)
plot(vpTrailOn and vpPocOn and not vpNewSess ? poc   : na, "VP · POC trail", color.new(C_POC, 65), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.price_scale)
plot(vpVwapOn ? vpVwap : na, "VP · Session VWAP", color.new(C_VWAP, 0), 1, plot.style_linebr, force_overlay = true, display = display.pane + display.price_scale)

// ── histogram (render aggregation into ≤110 rows) ─────────────────────────────
var array<box> vpBoxes = array.new<box>()
// Drawn by a function, out of the script's main body; it returns where the
// tag column starts.
f_vpRender() =>
    for b in vpBoxes
        box.delete(b)
    array.clear(vpBoxes)
    int tx = (vpHistOn ? vpRight : bar_index + VP_CONE) + VP_GUTTER
    if vpHistOn and not na(vpBin) and vpBin > 0 and pocVol > 0
        int maxRight = vpLeft
        int nB = array.size(vpKey)
        if nB > 0
            int ROWS_MAX = 110
            int step = math.max(1, int(math.ceil(nB / float(ROWS_MAX))))
            int nR   = int(math.ceil(nB / float(step)))
            array<float> rV  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rB  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rS  = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rLo = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<float> rHi = array.new<float>(nR, 0.0)
            array<bool>  rP  = array.new<bool>(nR, false)
            [pIdx, pFound] = f_vpLocate(vpKey, pocKey)
            for i = 0 to nB - 1
                int rr = int(math.floor(i / float(step)))
                array.set(rV, rr, array.get(rV, rr) + array.get(vpVol, i))
                array.set(rB, rr, array.get(rB, rr) + array.get(vpBuy, i))
                array.set(rS, rr, array.get(rS, rr) + array.get(vpSell, i))
                if i % step == 0
                    array.set(rLo, rr, array.get(vpKey, i) * vpBin)
                if i % step == step - 1 or i == nB - 1
                    array.set(rHi, rr, (array.get(vpKey, i) + 1.0) * vpBin)
                if pFound and i == pIdx
                    array.set(rP, rr, true)
            // Row width is normalised by the WIDEST RENDERED ROW, not by the raw
            // POC bin. Above ROWS_MAX bins the rows are aggregated in groups of
            // `step`, so an aggregated row holds several bins' worth and can
            // exceed pocVol — which made the histogram overshoot its declared
            // width by up to `step` times and drag the tag column off the screen
            // with it. Any session finer than 110 bins hit this.
            float rMax   = 0.0
            float hvMean = 0.0
            int   hvCnt  = 0
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                float tv0 = array.get(rV, r0)
                rMax := math.max(rMax, tv0)
                if tv0 > 0
                    hvMean += tv0
                    hvCnt  += 1
            hvMean := hvCnt > 0 ? hvMean / hvCnt : 0.0
            float hvVar = 0.0
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                float tv0 = array.get(rV, r0)
                if tv0 > 0
                    hvVar += math.pow(tv0 - hvMean, 2)
            float hvSd  = hvCnt > 0 ? math.sqrt(hvVar / hvCnt) : 0.0
            float hvnTh = hvMean + 1.2 * hvSd
            float lvnTh = hvMean - 0.6 * hvSd
            array<float> srtV = array.new<float>()
            for r0 = 0 to nR - 1
                if array.get(rV, r0) > 0
                    array.push(srtV, array.get(rV, r0))
            if array.size(srtV) > 10
                array.sort(srtV, order.ascending)
                lvnTh := array.get(srtV, math.max(0, int(math.floor(array.size(srtV) * 0.10))))
            for r = 0 to nR - 1
                if array.size(vpBoxes) >= 470
                    break
                float tV = array.get(rV, r)
                int wTot = tV > 0 and rMax > 0 ? int(math.round(inpVpWidth * tV / rMax)) : 0
                if wTot > 0
                    float yB    = array.get(rLo, r)
                    float ySpan = array.get(rHi, r) - yB
                    float yT    = yB + ySpan * 0.85
                    float pc    = yB + ySpan / 2.0
                    bool  isPoc = array.get(rP, r)
                    maxRight := math.max(maxRight, vpLeft + wTot)
                    bool inVa = not na(vah) and not na(vaLow) and pc >= vaLow and pc <= vah
                    int  fade = inVa ? 48 : 72
                    if vpMono
                        // MONOCHROME: one box per row, hue = identity never
                        // direction — amber POC row, blue value-area rows, grey
                        // out-of-value tails. POC row is a denser amber FILL.
                        color rowCol = isPoc ? C_POC : inVa ? C_VA : C_NODE
                        int   rowFd  = isPoc ? 25 : fade
                        array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(rowCol, rowFd), force_overlay = true))
                    else
                        // DELTA SPLIT: green inferred-buy / red inferred-sell, with
                        // the POC row marked by an amber OUTLINE so the split keeps
                        // its colour.
                        float bV = array.get(rB, r)
                        int   wB = tV > 0 ? int(math.round(wTot * bV / tV)) : 0
                        if wB > 0
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wB, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_UP, fade), force_overlay = true))
                        if wTot - wB > 0
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft + wB, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_DN, fade), force_overlay = true))
                        if isPoc
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft, yT, vpLeft + wTot, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = color.new(C_POC, 0), border_width = 1, bgcolor = na, force_overlay = true))
                    if vpNodesOn and r > 0 and r < nR - 1 and not isPoc and tV > 0
                        float vL = array.get(rV, r - 1)
                        float vR = array.get(rV, r + 1)
                        bool  peak   = tV > vL and tV > vR
                        bool  trough = tV < vL and tV < vR
                        // Node marks sit just LEFT of the histogram (vpLeft-2..vpLeft-1),
                        // so they travel with the profile's offset and keep a one-bar gap.
                        // HVN dense violet / LVN pale violet — disjoint from BOTH the
                        // monochrome grey tails and the delta-split green/red, so the
                        // colour reads in either style. Form still separates them:
                        // full-height block = node, centred tick = vacuum.
                        if tV >= hvnTh and peak
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft - 2, yT, vpLeft - 1, yB, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_HVN, 40), force_overlay = true))
                        else if tV <= lvnTh and trough
                            array.push(vpBoxes, box.new(vpLeft - 2, pc - vpBin * 0.08, vpLeft - 1, pc + vpBin * 0.08, xloc = xloc.bar_index, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_LVN, 40), force_overlay = true))
            if maxRight > vpLeft
                tx := maxRight + VP_GUTTER
    tx
if barstate.islast
    tagX := f_vpRender()

// ── right-edge tags and managed level lines · live tier, IB, prior session,
//    naked POCs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Rebuilt on the last bar by one function - out of the script's main body,
// whose length Pine caps - so every tag, line and box is kept in an array
// rather than a variable of its own. The live tags come first, as before, so
// the collision control seats them ahead of the prior session's.
var array<label> vpLvTags  = array.new<label>()
var array<line>  vpLvLines = array.new<line>()
var array<box>   vpLvBoxes = array.new<box>()
f_vpLevels() =>
    for lb in vpLvTags
        label.delete(lb)
    array.clear(vpLvTags)
    for ln in vpLvLines
        line.delete(ln)
    array.clear(vpLvLines)
    for bx in vpLvBoxes
        box.delete(bx)
    array.clear(vpLvBoxes)
    array.clear(tagRows)
    // Kasauti's own levels are seated first - the stops, then the cone's edges -
    // then the profile's, under the same collision control.
    bool coneTags = inpCone and coneOk
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), stopL,  "long stop",  C_DN,   coneTags))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), stopS,  "short stop", C_UP,   coneTags))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), upper,  str.tostring(inpCover / 2.0 + 50.0, "#") + "% below", C_CONE, coneTags))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), lower,  str.tostring(inpCover / 2.0 + 50.0, "#") + "% above", C_CONE, coneTags))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), poc,    "POC",  C_POC,    vpPocOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vah,    "VAH",  C_VA,     vpVaOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vaLow,  "VAL",  C_VA,     vpVaOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpVwap, "VWAP", C_VWAP,   vpVwapOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpIbh,  "IBH",  C_VIOLET, vpIbOn))
    array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), vpIbl,  "IBL",  C_VIOLET, vpIbOn))
    // Session-anchored. Pine refuses drawings placed more than 10,000 bars into
    // history; every x in this block is bounded by VP_XBACK well inside that. The
    // old bound of 400 cited max_bars_back, which does not govern drawings, and
    // cut session lines short on 24-hour 1-minute charts (1,440 bars a session).
    int xSess = math.max(math.max(not na(vpSessStart) ? vpSessStart : 0, bar_index - VP_XBACK), 0)
    if vpPocOn and not na(poc)
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, poc, tagX, poc, color = color.new(C_POC, 0), width = 2, force_overlay = true))
    if vpVaOn and not na(vah) and not na(vaLow)
        array.push(vpLvBoxes, box.new(xSess, vah, bar_index, vaLow, border_color = na, bgcolor = color.new(C_VA, 93), force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vah,   tagX, vah,   color = color.new(C_VA, 20), width = 1, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vaLow, tagX, vaLow, color = color.new(C_VA, 20), width = 1, force_overlay = true))
    if vpIbOn and not na(vpIbh)
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vpIbh, tagX, vpIbh, color = color.new(C_VIOLET, 20), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xSess, vpIbl, tagX, vpIbl, color = color.new(C_VIOLET, 20), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true))
    if vpPrevOn and not na(prevPoc)
        int xA = math.max(0, bar_index - 30)
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevPoc, tagX, prevPoc, color = color.new(C_POC, 55), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevVah, tagX, prevVah, color = color.new(C_VA, 55),  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(xA, prevVal, tagX, prevVal, color = color.new(C_VA, 55),  width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevPoc, "pPOC", C_POC, vpPrevOn))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevVah, "pVAH", C_VA,  vpPrevOn))
        array.push(vpLvTags, f_vpTag(label(na), prevVal, "pVAL", C_VA,  vpPrevOn))
    if vpNakedOn and array.size(vpNpY) > 0
        int xMinN = math.max(0, bar_index - math.min(inpVpNakedAge, VP_XBACK))
        int nN    = array.size(vpNpY)
        for i = 0 to nN - 1
            float ny = array.get(vpNpY, i)
            int   x1 = math.max(xMinN, array.get(vpNpX, i))
            array.push(vpLvLines, line.new(x1, ny, bar_index, ny, color = color.new(C_POC, 30), width = 1, style = line.style_dotted, force_overlay = true))
if barstate.islast
    f_vpLevels()

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  8 · THE PANE
//
//  The columns are the surprise, clipped at ±4 for display so the tapes keep
//  their place; the two lines are the learned bands it is judged against.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bool vSur = inpPane == "Surprise and tapes"
bool vPrf = inpPane == "Proof"

color cTr  = trRaw == 2 ? C_UP : trRaw == 0 ? C_DN : C_NEUT
color cCol = mU or mD ? color.new(cTr, 0) : color.new(cTr, 55)
plot(vSur ? math.max(-4.0, math.min(4.0, u)) : na, "Surprise (σ)", cCol, 1, plot.style_columns)
plot(vSur ? bU : na,              "Learned upper band",     color.new(C_CONE, 20), 1)
plot(vSur ? -bD : na,             "Learned lower band",     color.new(C_CONE, 20), 1)
plot(vSur ? 0.0 : na,             "Zero",                   color.new(C_NEUT, 60), 1)

plot(vPrf and nP > 0 ? 100.0 * math.log(eqF) : na, "Following the dial (log %)", color.new(C_CONE, 0), 2)
plot(vPrf and nP > 0 ? 100.0 * math.log(eqH) : na, "Buy and hold (log %)",       color.new(C_NEUT, 20), 1)

// ── the tapes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Four bands of columns, one per bar. Inner pair: what the cone and the dial
// listen to. Outer pair: where each is heading. A tape with no reading yet is
// neutral grey.
const float TAPE_Y = 4.9
const float MOM_Y  = 5.6
const float TAPE_H = 0.28
bool tapesOn = vSur and inpTapes

// TREND · hue is the side; faint while flat, a step at ±0.5σ, solid by 1.5σ.
float tAbs  = math.abs(T)
color tHue  = T >= 0.0 ? C_UP : C_DN
color tapeT = na(T) ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : tAbs < 0.5 ? color.from_gradient(tAbs, 0.0, 0.5, color.new(tHue, 90), color.new(tHue, 62)) :
     color.from_gradient(tAbs, 0.5, 1.5, color.new(tHue, 40), color.new(tHue, 0))

// STRETCH LADDER · hue is the side it leans; intensity is how many rungs are
// outside their own cone on that side.
color lHue  = ladX >= 0.0 ? C_UP : C_DN
color tapeL = not ladOk ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : ladN >= 3 ? color.new(lHue, 0) : ladN >= 1 ? color.new(lHue, 40) :
     color.from_gradient(math.abs(ladX), 0.0, 1.0, color.new(lHue, 92), color.new(lHue, 66))

// RISK · blue calm, grey normal, gold stressed; deeper toward either end.
color tapeR = not regOk ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : regRaw == 0 ? color.from_gradient(prk, 0.0, 100.0 / 3.0, color.new(C_CONE, 15), color.new(C_CONE, 60)) :
     regRaw == 2 ? color.from_gradient(prk, 200.0 / 3.0, 100.0, color.new(C_GOLD, 45), color.new(C_GOLD, 0)) : color.new(C_NEUT, 70)

// RISK MOMENTUM · gold rising, blue falling, faint steady.
float rmAbs = math.abs(rMom)
color tapeM = na(rMom) ? color.new(C_NEUT, 82) : rmS == 2 ? color.from_gradient(rmAbs, 0.10, 0.40, color.new(C_GOLD, 40), color.new(C_GOLD, 0)) :
     rmS == 0 ? color.from_gradient(rmAbs, 0.10, 0.40, color.new(C_CONE, 45), color.new(C_CONE, 10)) : color.new(C_NEUT, 86)

plot(tapesOn ?  TAPE_Y + TAPE_H : na, "Trend tape",          tapeT, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase =  TAPE_Y - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ?  MOM_Y  + TAPE_H : na, "Stretch ladder tape", tapeL, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase =  MOM_Y  - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ? -TAPE_Y + TAPE_H : na, "Risk tape",           tapeR, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase = -TAPE_Y - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)
plot(tapesOn ? -MOM_Y  + TAPE_H : na, "Risk momentum tape",  tapeM, 1, plot.style_columns, histbase = -MOM_Y  - TAPE_H, display = display.pane)

// What each tape says, in words - for the labels and the table.
string trTxt  = na(T) ? "warming" : (trRaw == 2 ? "up " : trRaw == 0 ? "down " : "flat ") + f_num(T, "+0.0;-0.0") + "σ"
string ladTxt = not ladOk ? "warming" : ladUp == 0 and ladDn == 0 ? "inside at all four horizons" :
     (ladUp > 0 ? str.tostring(ladUp) + " of 4 above" : "") + (ladUp > 0 and ladDn > 0 ? " · " : "") + (ladDn > 0 ? str.tostring(ladDn) + " of 4 below" : "")
string regTxt = not regOk ? "learning" : regRaw == 0 ? "calm" : regRaw == 2 ? "stressed" : "normal"
string rmTxt  = na(rMom) ? "warming" : rmS == 2 ? "rising " + f_pct(math.exp(rMom) - 1.0, "+#;-#") + " · spikes fade" : rmS == 0 ? "falling " + f_pct(math.exp(rMom) - 1.0, "+#;-#") : "steady"

// ── on the price chart ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
plot(inpLand ? upper[inpH] : na,  "Landing band · upper",   color.new(C_CONE, 45), 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(inpLand ? lower[inpH] : na,  "Landing band · lower",   color.new(C_CONE, 45), 1, force_overlay = true)
plot(inpTrail ? stopL : na,       "Long stop history",      color.new(C_DN, 55), 1, plot.style_stepline, force_overlay = true)
plot(inpTrail ? stopS : na,       "Short stop history",     color.new(C_UP, 55), 1, plot.style_stepline, force_overlay = true)
plotshape(inpMark and provenUp,   "Entered a proven state · positive", shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, C_UP, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)
plotshape(inpMark and provenDn,   "Entered a proven state · negative", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, C_DN, size = size.tiny, force_overlay = true)

// ── the forward cone, and the tapes' names at the pane's right edge ───────
// The cone's and the stops' tags sit in the profile's tag column (section 7),
// so one collision control seats every tag on the price chart.
var polyline plCone = na
var line     lnL    = na
var line     lnS    = na
var array<label> lbs = array.new<label>()

f_tapeTag(float py, string txt, color c) =>
    label.new(bar_index + 2, py, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_index, color = color.new(c, 100), style = label.style_label_left,
         textcolor = c, size = size.small)

if barstate.islast
    polyline.delete(plCone)
    line.delete(lnL)
    line.delete(lnS)
    while array.size(lbs) > 0
        label.delete(array.pop(lbs))
    if inpCone and coneOk
        array<chart.point> pts = array.new<chart.point>()
        for i = 0 to inpH
            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(bar_index + i, close * math.exp(qU * sig * math.sqrt(i))))
        for i = inpH to 0
            array.push(pts, chart.point.from_index(bar_index + i, close * math.exp(-qD * sig * math.sqrt(i))))
        plCone := polyline.new(pts, curved = false, closed = true, xloc = xloc.bar_index, line_color = color.new(C_CONE, 30),
             fill_color = color.new(C_CONE, 88), line_width = 1, force_overlay = true)
        lnL := line.new(bar_index, stopL, bar_index + inpH, stopL, color = color.new(C_DN, 20), style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true)
        lnS := line.new(bar_index, stopS, bar_index + inpH, stopS, color = color.new(C_UP, 20), style = line.style_dashed, force_overlay = true)
    if tapesOn
        array.push(lbs, f_tapeTag((TAPE_Y + MOM_Y) / 2.0, "TREND " + trTxt + "  ·  LADDER " + ladTxt, na(T) ? C_NEUT : tHue))
        array.push(lbs, f_tapeTag(-(TAPE_Y + MOM_Y) / 2.0, "RISK " + regTxt + "  ·  " + rmTxt, regRaw == 2 or rmS == 2 ? C_GOLD : C_NEUT))

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  9 · THE TABLE
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
f_stName(int s) =>
    string a = s < 3 ? "trend down" : s < 6 ? "trend flat" : "trend up"
    string b = s % 3 == 0 ? "broke below the cone" : s % 3 == 2 ? "broke above the cone" : "inside the cone"
    a + " · " + b

f_row(table t, int rw, string k, string val, color c, string tip) =>
    table.cell(t, 0, rw, k,   text_color = C_NEUT, text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left, tooltip = tip)
    table.cell(t, 1, rw, val, text_color = c,      text_size = size.small, text_halign = text.align_left, tooltip = tip)

var table tb = na
if inpTbl and barstate.islast
    if na(tb)
        tb := table.new(inpPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right : inpPos == "Bottom right" ? position.bottom_right :
             inpPos == "Top left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_left, 2, 10, bgcolor = C_PANEL,
             frame_color = color.new(C_NEUT, 70), frame_width = 1, border_color = color.new(C_NEUT, 88), border_width = 1,
             force_overlay = true)
    string hTxt = str.tostring(inpH) + " bars"
    if na(sig)
        f_row(tb, 0, "KASAUTI", "warming · needs " + str.tostring(WARM + inpH) + " bars, has " + str.tostring(bar_index + 1), C_GOLD,
             "The risk forecast needs a year of bars before its first reading.")
    else
        f_row(tb, 0, "RISK", "±" + f_pct(sH, "#.0") + " over " + hTxt + " (1σ) · " + f_pct(sig * math.sqrt(bpy), "#") + " a year · " + regTxt + " · " + rmTxt,
             regRaw == 2 or rmS == 2 ? C_GOLD : C_TEXT, "The forecast size of one standard move over the horizon; the same risk annualised from this chart's own bar count; the RISK tape - where it stands among its last 500 bars; and RISK MOMENTUM - its change over the last " + hTxt + ". Measured: stressed risk falls back, calm risk persists, and a rise of more than 10% was lower again " + hTxt + " later three times in four.")
        f_row(tb, 1, "CONE " + str.tostring(inpCover, "#") + "%", f_px(lower) + "  to  " + f_px(upper) + "   (" + f_pct(lower / close - 1.0, "+#.0;-#.0") + " / " + f_pct(upper / close - 1.0, "+#.0;-#.0") + ")", C_CONE,
             "Where the close should be " + hTxt + " from now, with the stated probability. The two sides are learned separately and listen to the risk and trend tapes, so the cone need not be symmetric.")
        float dL = 1.0 - stopL / close
        float dS = stopS / close - 1.0
        f_row(tb, 2, "LONG STOP", f_px(stopL) + " (−" + f_pct(dL, "#.0") + ") · size " + f_pct(inpRisk / 100.0 / dL, "#") + " of equity", ladDn >= 3 ? C_GOLD : C_DN,
             "Touched within " + hTxt + " on " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + "% of occasions. SIZE is the position that loses " + str.tostring(inpRisk) + "% of equity if it is. GOLD while three or four ladder rungs are below their cones: there, measured, a long stop was touched about a quarter of the time, not a fifth.")
        f_row(tb, 3, "SHORT STOP", f_px(stopS) + " (+" + f_pct(dS, "#.0") + ") · size " + f_pct(inpRisk / 100.0 / dS, "#") + " of equity", C_UP,
             "The mirror: touched within " + hTxt + " on " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + "% of occasions.")
        f_row(tb, 4, "EXPOSURE", "hold " + f_num(E, "0.00") + "×   ·   dial " + f_num(dial, "0.00") + " = risk " + f_num(dialR, "0.00") + (inpMode == "Risk only" ? "" : " × trend " + f_num(dialT, "0.00")), C_TEXT,
             "HOLD is the position to carry: the dial, followed only in steps. RISK: this instrument's average risk over its risk now, capped. TREND: the throttle, from the floor in a full downtrend to 1 in a full uptrend. Measured on daily and weekly bars; on hourly bars the dial lost to buy and hold.")
        f_row(tb, 5, "TAPES", "trend " + trTxt + " · ladder " + ladTxt, na(T) ? C_NEUT : tHue,
             "TREND: the move over a quarter, a half and a year of bars, in σ. The cone's skew and the dial's throttle listen to it. LADDER: how many of the four horizons (" + str.tostring(h0) + ", " + str.tostring(inpH) + ", " + str.tostring(h2) + ", " + str.tostring(h3) + " bars) closed outside their own learned cone. Three or four on one side happens on about 4% of bars. It carries no measured direction.")
        string ledTxt = st < 0 ? "—" : f_stName(st) + "\n" + (na(lZ) ? "seen " + f_num(lNe, "#") + " times · too few to judge" :
             "seen " + f_num(lNe, "#") + " times · next " + hTxt + " " + f_num(lMu, "+0.00;-0.00") + "σ against " + f_num(gM, "+0.00;-0.00") + "σ usual · " +
             (proven == 1 ? "PROVEN positive" : proven == -1 ? "PROVEN negative" : "unproven") + " (z " + f_num(lZ, "+0.0;-0.0") + ", believed edge " + f_num(lPost, "+0.00;-0.00") + "σ)")
        f_row(tb, 6, "STATE", ledTxt, proven == 1 ? C_UP : proven == -1 ? C_DN : C_TEXT,
             "The state this bar is in, and what THIS CHART's history says followed it: the next " + hTxt + ", in σ, against the chart's own usual. UNPROVEN means the difference is not distinguishable from chance - which is the normal reading.")
        float cov = nF > 0 ? 1.0 - (nMU + nMD) / nF : na
        f_row(tb, 7, "CALIBRATION", "cone held " + f_pct(cov, "#.0") + " (last 250: " + f_pct(covRecent, "#") + ", target " + str.tostring(inpCover, "#") + ") · stops touched " + f_pct(nF > 0 ? nMS / nF : na, "#.0") + " / " + f_pct(nF > 0 ? nMR / nF : na, "#.0") +
             " (target " + str.tostring(inpStop, "#") + ") · " + str.tostring(nF) + " forecasts", math.abs(cov - inpCover / 100.0) > 0.03 ? C_GOLD : C_TEXT,
             "The record of every forecast this chart has settled, and of the last 250. Gold when the cone is more than 3 points from its target - usually a short history.")
        f_row(tb, 8, "PROOF · dial", "Sharpe " + f_num(shF, "0.00") + " · worst drawdown " + f_pct(ddF, "#") + " · " + f_pct(cagF, "#.0") + " a year", C_CONE,
             "Following the exposure dial on this chart, one bar late, net of costs, since the first reading.")
        f_row(tb, 9, "PROOF · hold", "Sharpe " + f_num(shH, "0.00") + " · worst drawdown " + f_pct(ddH, "#") + " · " + f_pct(cagH, "#.0") + " a year", C_NEUT,
             "Buy and hold over the same bars.")

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALERTS
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
alertcondition(mU and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · closed above the cone",
     message = "The close landed above the cone drawn H bars ago - a move the forecast gave about one chance in ten at the default coverage. A surprise, not a signal.")
alertcondition(mD and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · closed below the cone",
     message = "The close landed below the cone drawn H bars ago - a move the forecast gave about one chance in ten at the default coverage. A surprise, not a signal.")
alertcondition(ladOk and ladUp >= 3 and not (ladUp[1] >= 3) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · ladder break above",
     message = "Three or four horizons of the stretch ladder have closed above their own cones - about 4% of bars. No measured direction.")
alertcondition(ladOk and ladDn >= 3 and not (ladDn[1] >= 3) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · ladder break below",
     message = "Three or four horizons of the stretch ladder have closed below their own cones - about 4% of bars. Measured: a long stop here is touched about a quarter of the time, not a fifth.")
alertcondition(regRaw == 2 and regRaw[1] != 2 and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · risk tape stressed",
     message = "Forecast risk has entered the top third of its last 500 bars. The cone and stops are wider and the exposure dial lower.")
alertcondition(rmS == 2 and rmS[1] != 2 and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · risk rising",
     message = "Forecast risk is more than 10% above where it stood H bars ago. Measured: after such a rise risk was lower again H bars later about three times in four.")
alertcondition(E != E[1] and not na(E[1]) and barstate.isconfirmed, title = "Kasauti · exposure changed",
     message = "The exposure dial has moved a full step from the position held. The table's EXPOSURE row carries the new position.")
alertcondition(provenUp, title = "Kasauti · entered a proven state (positive)",
     message = "The chart entered a state its own history has proven positive: the next H bars beat the chart's usual by more than two posterior σ.")
alertcondition(provenDn, title = "Kasauti · entered a proven state (negative)",
     message = "The chart entered a state its own history has proven negative: the next H bars trailed the chart's usual by more than two posterior σ.")
